-//   * Gemma4 26B-A4B Q8_0 `-ncmoe 20` + an external MTP head: 512 MiB per auxiliary context.
+// ONE PINNED COMPUTE REGION PER AUXILIARY CONTEXT (the maintainer's decision, 2026-11-24): the charge is a COUNT
+// times a per-context size, not a single lump for "the pair", because every auxiliary context that arrives after
+// the arena is sized needs one region of its own and a pair may carry more than one (the decode arm, and the
+// drafter's context).  Which term charges which context is stated in the derivation below: the drafter's region
+// comes out of the draft reserve (`common_draft_reserve_derive()`, derived or flat, and always non-zero when a
+// drafter has a context), so counting it again here would spend ~1.3 GiB of arena for nothing -- 4864 MiB of
+// reserve on the measured shape, against 3584 + 1280 that the two regions and the draft's KV actually need.
+//
+// MEASURED (2026-11-23/24, `GGML_CUDA_WORK_ALLOC_DEBUG=1`): an auxiliary context's COMPUTE buffer is one narrow
+// layout, and it is what a region has to cover -- the slab maps it from the VA it leaves unmapped, so no arena
+// table has to be evicted at load to make room:
+//   * 35B-A3B Q8_0 `-ncmoe 40`, np 4 + `draft-mtp-adaptive` n_max 7 (host expert tier, slab armed): the DECODE
+//     ARM 1280 MiB at its verify width (`4 x (7+1)` = 32 rows), the DRAFT 512 MiB -- i.e. exactly one region per
+//     auxiliary context;
+//   * Gemma4 26B-A4B Q8_0 `-ncmoe 20` + its MTP head: 512 MiB for the draft's region (the pair refuses this
+//     shape: a gemma4 assistant shares the target's KV).
 // The earlier "+157/+235 MiB per device" figure (27B/Q8_0/3-GPU tensor) measured the *arena shrink after the
 // slab had already absorbed the buffer*, i.e. a different quantity -- a dense model arms no slab at all, so
 // that arm could not see the real number.  THIS IS AN APPROXIMATION: the exact per-device figure is known only
 // once the decode arm's own `sched_reserve` has run, and the slab logs a one-time recommendation for the next
-// run at that point (`ggml_cuda_slab_aux_commit_locked`).  Withholding the widest measured value means the pin
-// never has to evict on any validated shape; an over-estimate only costs arena on a shape whose aux layout is
-// narrower, which the logged recommendation then fixes.
-static const int COMMON_ARMS_RESERVE_MIB = 1280;
+// run at that point (`ggml_cuda_slab_aux_commit_locked`, which after r377-wip states the sum for EVERY region).
+// Withholding the widest measured value means the pin never has to evict on any validated shape; an over-estimate
+// only costs arena on a shape whose aux layout is narrower, which the logged recommendation then fixes.  A shape
+// whose verify batch is much wider than 32 rows (a large `-np` at a large `--spec-draft-n-max`) should be
+// re-measured, because the layout grows with that width.
+static const int COMMON_ARMS_RESERVE_MIB_PER_AUX = 1280;
+
+// The auxiliary contexts this configuration creates that need a pinned compute region charged HERE: the decode arm,
+// and any further decode-band context (`n_aux` is a count so a third one is charged when one is added).  A
+// drafter's context is auxiliary too, but its region is the draft reserve's term -- see the block above.
+struct common_arms_reserve {
+    int    n_aux = 0;    // auxiliary contexts charged by this term
+    size_t bytes = 0;    // what the arena holds back for them
+    bool   charged = false;
+};
+
+static common_arms_reserve common_arms_reserve_derive(const common_params & params) {
+    common_arms_reserve res;
+    if (params.prefill_decode_arms_mode == COMMON_ARMS_OFF) {
+        return res;
+    }
+    const char * why = common_arms_pair_possible(params);
+    if (why != nullptr) {
+        return res;   // refused: charge NOTHING (DESIGN V2)
+    }
+    res.n_aux   = 1;   // the decode arm
+    res.bytes   = (size_t) res.n_aux * (size_t) COMMON_ARMS_RESERVE_MIB_PER_AUX * 1024 * 1024;
+    res.charged = true;
+    return res;
+}
 
